    "_comment": "Map art (client only). themes: one per kind of area; areaThemes picks one by area id, else by kind (town | open | dungeon). sheet = a Flare tileset (tile ids are Flare's). floor = weights of the floor tiles (random per cell, the same every time). Dungeon-like themes: a wall cell next to the floor shows wallE when the floor is east of it (+x, down-right on screen: its face looks at the room), wallS when it is south (+y), and wallBack otherwise (walls between the camera and the room; they turn see-through when the hero is behind). backAlpha = opacity of wallBack (0–255). Open themes: grass under everything (under = true) and props (trees, rocks) on wall cells; propChance = chance by distance to the nearest floor (1, 2, 3 cells), dense at the edge so blocked ground reads as blocked. objects: map features (tile on a sheet, or a look for NPCs); 'flat' ones lie on the floor, the others are sorted with the actors; scale shrinks Flare's big set pieces to our cells; a theme can override an object. objectScale: props and objects are 1/3 of Flare's size, like the tiles. exitClearance: no trees or rocks within this many cells of an exit, so its sign and glowing zone stay in sight.",
